            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for to be scattered, then the Hindi for the floating of lamps."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कथा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कथा — kathā — \"a tale; a sacred story\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दादी हर रात एक नई कथा सुनाती थीं। dādī har rāt ek naī kathā sunātī thīṁ. Grandmother used to tell a new tale every night."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कथा (kathā) is Sanskrit kathā, \"a story, a conversation\" (Monier-Williams). Beside कहानी, it is the old or sacred tale."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
